  "notes": [
    {
      "note": "# Genuary 5\n\n> Write \u201cGenuary\u201d. Avoid using a font.\n\n\nThis Graph uses an Environment to render with reflections\n\nInside the Environment node is \n\n* A Cursor node which tracks where the mouse is\n* Math to convert the mouse coordinate to world unit coordinates\n* Nodes that convert the resulting 3d position into a Queue (array) of transforms to send to a Mesh\n* The Mesh draws a PBR Shader along with a \u201cSuper Shape\u201d which is a mathematical 3D shade defined by numbers\n* Those numbers animate over time\n\nYou can write in \u2018digital grafitti\u2019 Genuary!\n\n\n> Hint\n\n* You have to load your own EXR HDRI image to get the environment to reflect something. Try searching for free HDRI\u2019s and see how the composition changes.",
      "id": "683C9AEF-E351-456A-92C3-60087A79121C",
